{"id": "xczechia", "name": "Sumava National Park", "short": "Sumava", "place": "Czechia", "lat": 49.0, "lon": 13.5, "side": "r", "cont": "Europe", "country": "Czechia", "kind": "Forest", "park": true, "blurb": "Spruce forest, bark beetles and the returned lynx of the Bohemian Forest.", "tip": {"id": "lynx", "title": "Remove the lynx", "text": "Lynx hunt roe deer, red deer and foxes. Set Eurasian lynx to -100% and watch roe deer, then the bilberry and young trees they browse."}, "sources": [{"title": "Wikipedia: Sumava National Park", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/%C5%A0umava_National_Park"}, {"title": "Wikipedia: Bohemian Forest", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bohemian_Forest"}, {"title": "Wikipedia: Eurasian lynx", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eurasian_lynx"}, {"title": "Wikipedia: Ips typographus", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ips_typographus"}, {"title": "Wikipedia: Norway spruce", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Norway_spruce"}], "notes": "The species list comes from GBIF occurrence records inside a circle around the park, so it can include nearby areas. Feeding links come from GloBI records and the sources listed where they state them; others are general ecology and are illustrative.", "imgwiki": "Šumava National Park", "icon": "whitebark", "tier": "overview", "nodes": [{"id": "sun", "sp": "sunlight", "xh": 0.08, "desc": "Light reaching the forest floor limits the growth of berries, seedlings and mountain meadows beneath the canopy."}, {"id": "water", "sp": "peat bogs and streams", "xh": 0.3}, {"id": "soil", "sp": "forest soil and deadwood", "xh": 0.5}, {"id": "decomp", "sp": "decomposer community", "xh": 0.9, "desc": "Break down fallen leaves, beetle-killed spruce and carcasses, returning nutrients to the soil."}, {"id": "spruce", "sp": "picea abies", "xh": 0.1, "desc": "Dominant conifer of the Bohemian Forest, widely planted. Spruce stands stressed by wind or drought are the main host of the spruce bark beetle.", "badge": "Foundation species"}, {"id": "beech", "sp": "fagus sylvatica", "xh": 0.28, "desc": "A broadleaf tree of the lower and middle slopes. Its nuts feed wild boar and rodents.", "no": ["badge"]}, {"id": "birch", "sp": "betula pendula", "xh": 0.46}, {"id": "rowan", "sp": "sorbus aucuparia", "xh": 0.64}, {"id": "bilberry", "sp": "vaccinium myrtillus", "xh": 0.84, "desc": "Low shrub of the forest floor. Its leaves and berries feed deer, and martens take the fruit."}, {"id": "beetle", "sp": "ips typographus", "xh": 0.08, "name": "Eurasian spruce bark beetle", "wiki": "Ips typographus", "desc": "Breeds under spruce bark and can overwhelm stressed trees in outbreaks, a major natural disturbance in Sumava.", "badge": "Ecosystem engineer"}, {"id": "roe", "sp": "capreolus capreolus", "xh": 0.24, "desc": "A small browsing deer that eats leaves, shoots and berries of trees and shrubs; the preferred prey of lynx where common."}, {"id": "red", "sp": "cervus elaphus", "xh": 0.4, "name": "Red deer", "wiki": "Red deer", "desc": "The largest deer of the forest. It grazes grasses, browses shrubs such as bilberry and is prey for wolves and lynx.", "ic": "elk"}, {"id": "boar", "sp": "sus scrofa", "xh": 0.56, "desc": "Omnivore that roots for nuts, plants, small animals and carrion in the forest."}, {"id": "beaver", "sp": "castor fiber", "xh": 0.72}, {"id": "mouse", "sp": "apodemus flavicollis", "xh": 0.88, "desc": "A forest rodent that eats seeds and small invertebrates; prey for foxes, martens and buzzards."}, {"id": "woodpecker", "sp": "dendrocopos major", "xh": 0.12, "desc": "Splits bark to reach insect larvae, so it can help limit bark beetle numbers."}, {"id": "marten", "sp": "martes martes", "xh": 0.3}, {"id": "fox", "sp": "vulpes vulpes", "xh": 0.5, "desc": "Adaptable predator and scavenger that eats rodents, birds, carrion and fruit."}, {"id": "buzzard", "sp": "buteo buteo", "xh": 0.7, "desc": "Hawk that hunts rodents and other small animals over forest edges and clearings."}, {"i